<<~ ahu slot=`#/contract`>>

!! Boot Gate

`bootTrustedModules(tw, preloaded, granted)` runs after TW5's own boot resolves. It queries every tiddler that WEARS the tw5-module component — `[all[tiddlers]stack:has[lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/tw5/tw5-module]]`, the has-stack model — and admits each one only after it clears the trust layers below. An admitted tiddler re-enters the wiki as `type: application/javascript` carrying the `module-type` its own field names, defaulting to `library`, with its tags stripped.

''This code cannot load from a meme.'' It needs a live `$tw` instance and stands as the mechanism that promotes memes into executables.

''A gate that throws admits nothing more.'' The whole query sits under a `catch` that falls through, so a wiki whose filter surface has not landed injects nothing rather than failing the boot, and a throw mid-walk stops the walk: modules already admitted stand, no later title joins. The gate fails closed.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/thresholds`>>

!! Gate Layers

| Layer | Reading | Floor |
|---|---|---|
| preload | the title came in with the genesis preload | — |
| grant | the title sits in the granted set: the promote ledger's hand-committed digest, held on this device, not shadowed by kāpae; absent means refused and warned | — |
| body | non-empty text, and not the injected-body placeholder | — |
| digest | `source-sha256` verifies through `SubtleCrypto.digest("SHA-256")` | — |
| type | `module-type` reads `library`; any other type refuses by name | — |

''The digest read accepts two spellings.'' A `source-sha256` field may ride bare (implicit sha256) or tagged (`sha256:…`); `digestsEqual` normalizes both, so a reader accepting both stands BEFORE any emitter starts writing the tagged form.

No field value on a carrier authorizes execution, and the gate fails closed. A keyhive capability proof stands as a layer still owed; the gate admits on grant, digest and type.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/aggregate`>>

!! The Aggregate Define

Each admitted module defines under its own title: `tw.modules.define(title, "library", text)`, the name another module `require`s.

<<~/ahu>>

